<LearnLayout
  title="Archive: Put Work Aside Without Losing It — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How archiving keeps a finished Quest, Project, or Area hidden but kept — manually or automatically."
  path="/learn/archive"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Archive: put work aside without losing it</h1>
  <p>
    Archiving is "hidden but kept" — distinct from marking a Quest done and
    distinct from Trash. An archived Quest, Project, or Area drops out of
    your everyday list without being deleted; unarchive it whenever you need
    it again. Archiving a Project cascades to archive its child Quests;
    unarchiving does not cascade back.
  </p>
  <p>
    A Quest also archives itself automatically once it's done and hasn't
    shown up in any session for a configurable stretch of time (30 days by
    default) — the passive version of tidying up, so finished work doesn't
    sit in your active list forever just because you forgot to put it away.
  </p>
  <p>
    Today that's one fixed rule. Richer automatic-archival rules — different
    thresholds per Area, archiving by staleness regardless of status, and
    similar — are still being defined.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
